   "rule_summary": "Each model shall undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C before certification and at least annually thereafter, using a regulator-approved protocol and representative units. A model with a failure rate above 5% shall be subject to a regulator-approved corrective-action plan and retesting; continued sales may proceed while the plan is followed unless the regulator determines suspension is necessary to protect the public.",
   "comparison": "weakened by: over_limit_consequence, transition",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model shall undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C before certification and at least annually thereafter, using a regulator-approved protocol and representative units. Manufacturers shall provide per-model test methods, sample sizes, and results to the regulator and to customers who buy that model. Individual-company per-model failure rates need not be published to the general public; regulators may publish aggregated industry results. A model with a failure rate above 5% shall be subject to a regulator-approved corrective-action plan and retesting; continued sales may proceed while the plan is followed unless the regulator determines suspension is necessary to protect the public. Manufacturers shall promptly notify affected customers of any safety hazard and actions they need to take."
  },
